<title>ITALY: ALPINE SKIING-ITALY'S KOSTNER WINS WOMEN'S SUPER-G.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-ITALY'S KOSTNER WINS WOMEN'S SUPER-G.</headline>
<dateline>SESTRIERE, Italy 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Isolde Kostner of Italy won the women's super-giant slalom gold medal at the Alpine skiing world championships on Tuesday in one minute 23.50 seconds, according to provisional results. </p>
<p>Katja Seizinger of Germany took the silver in 1:23.58 and compatriot Hilde Gerg the bronze in 1:23.64.</p>
